3. MANDATORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC INTEGRITY & PASSPHRASE ENFORCEMENT CONDITION
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
To prevent cryptographic downgrade attacks and protect end-user security across
the OpenQPEP ecosystem, any Covered Work or Derivative Work that reads, writes,
generates, or claims interoperability with OpenQPEP packets or .qpkrf (Quantum
Proof Key Ring File) files MUST strictly preserve:
  (a) The non-bypassable QPKD-Argon Passphrase Policy requiring every passphrase
      to be at least twelve (12) characters in length and contain at least two
      (2) numeric digits, four (4) special characters, two (2) uppercase
      letters, and four (4) lowercase letters;
  (b) The atomic .qpkrf conjunctive self-certification signature and
      integrity_mac verification checks;
  (c) Attached-only signature encapsulation (prohibiting detached signatures);
  (d) Dual-stream CC-512 authenticated frame integrity and final-chunk
      truncation verification.

Derivative Works that strip or weaken these security guarantees MUST NOT use the
names "OpenQPEP", "Calyx QPEP", "Calyx QPEP Client", or the ".qpkrf" extension.

